course: dictionary
lesson: 14443
title: Pallor: a face that has lost its colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a face looks. Pallor is a noun. It names an unhealthy paleness of the face or skin. «When Mum saw the pallor on Ben's cheeks, she called the doctor.» The clue is that Mum is worried. Something is wrong with Ben.
explain: Pallor can come from illness, fear, shock or tiredness. «After the loud crash, her pallor made her freckles stand out.» A shock can drain the colour from a face, so pallor fits. Ask yourself: does this skin look pale in a way that seems unwell?
explain: Pallor is a strong, slightly formal word. Writers use it to make a character look ill, scared or ghostly. Plain pale is an everyday word. «Her face was pale» is simple, while «a deathly pallor» says much more.
fact: Pallor means unhealthy paleness of the face or skin.
fact: Pallor can be caused by illness, fear, shock or tiredness.
fact: Pallor is an uncountable noun, so you say some pallor, not a pallor.
fact: «A deathly pallor» means a very pale, ghostly look, like someone who is very ill.
fact: Doctors and nurses notice pallor because it can be a sign of illness or blood loss.
exercise: «After the bad news, Sam's face had a sudden pallor.» What does pallor mean? | A bright red blush | *Unhealthy paleness, from shock | A loud shout | A sunny tan from the beach
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the unhealthy paleness: «The nurse noticed the pallor on his cheeks and checked his temperature.» | nurse | temperature | *pallor | cheeks
exercise: Ella says pallor is just a fancy word for red. Why is she wrong? | Pallor means red, because blushing shows colour | Pallor is a type of food | Pallor means very loud | *Pallor means pale, not red
test: What could cause the pallor in «The old man had a grey pallor after his long night shift.»? | *Tiredness, or being unwell | Eating too much cake | Laughing at a joke | Running a race in the sun
test: Which sentence uses pallor correctly? | *«The shock left her face with a deathly pallor.» | «The sky had a bright pallor of sunshine.» | «The cat ate her pallor for breakfast.» | «He hit the ball with a big pallor.»
exam: Which description fits pallor best? | *A pale, unhealthy look to the skin | A sudden rush of pink in the cheeks | A dark sunburn | A happy, shiny face
